    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T20:11:49Z",
    "body": "Work landed locally on issue/89-drill-prior-removal (d854733): new `operation/drill_prior.rs` - #96's PriorPlan simulated lazily (only when the raw-stock reading would refuse, shared with verify's acquittal); the reach depth, the R-plane law and the holder check read min(raw stock, prior surface) over the tool/holder disc; a counterbore an earlier op cut reads as air; lathe axial drills read the grid revolved about the axis. Unknown or tilted removal = raw stock; cross drills stay on raw stock (the column grid can't be read along a radial line). Drill's stamp carries the ahead-ops digest, so a drill goes Stale when an op ahead changes. Tests: drill_prior (8: pocket floor posts, faced R posts, lathe axial after facing, stale on a shallower pocket; raw-stock guards still refused). Lathe Facing can't face a stock allowance -> #122.",
